---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getAllCities } from '../lib/cities';
const cities = getAllCities();
const total = cities.reduce((s, c) => s + c.count, 0);
const site = 'https://toiletsnearme.pages.dev';
---
<Base
  title="About — Toilets Near Me"
  description="What Toilets Near Me is, where its data comes from, how the maps work, and how to report a facility that has changed."
  canonical={site + '/about/'}
  jsonld={[{ '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'AboutPage', name: 'About — Toilets Near Me', url: site + '/about/' }]}
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">About</span></nav>
      <h1>About Toilets Near Me</h1>
      <p class="lead">A live map of public toilets and washrooms across Indian cities — one clear answer, no signup.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap prose">
    <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
    <p>
      Finding a clean, working public toilet in an unfamiliar Indian city is harder than it should be. Listings are
      scattered, details are stale, and there is rarely a clear answer on whether a facility is free, paid, open now,
      or accessible. This site puts every mapped facility for a city on one map and lets you filter for what you
      actually need.
    </p>

    <h2>Where the data comes from</h2>
    <p>
      All locations come from OpenStreetMap, the community-maintained map of the world, used under the ODbL licence.
      {total.toLocaleString('en-IN')} facilities across {cities.length} cities are currently mapped here.
    </p>
    <p>
      Counts on each city page are computed directly from the OpenStreetMap tags on those facilities — free, paid,
      24-hour, wheelchair access, women's sections, baby changing. If a feature is not recorded on a facility we do not
      infer it: a missing tag means "not recorded yet", not "not available".
    </p>

    <h2>How the maps work</h2>
    <p>
      Each city page loads that city's facility data and draws it with Leaflet over OpenStreetMap tiles. Pins are
      grouped when you zoom out and separate as you zoom in. Tap a pin to see what is recorded for that facility, or
      use "Use my location" to centre the map on where you are. Directions open the exact spot in OpenStreetMap.
    </p>

    <h2>Reporting a problem</h2>
    <p>
      Facility details change — toilets close, move, or start charging. If something is wrong, the fastest fix is to
      correct it on OpenStreetMap itself, which fixes it for every map that uses the data, including this one.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Email <a href="mailto:skmstudio.services@gmail.com">skmstudio.services@gmail.com</a>.</p>
    <p class="fineprint">Data © OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open Database Licence.</p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-hero { background: radial-gradient(700px 240px at 20% -20%, var(--color-mint) 0%, transparent 70%); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line); padding: 30px 0 26px; }
  .crumbs { display: flex; gap: 8px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--color-muted); }
  .crumbs a { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .page-hero h1 { margin: 10px 0 0; font-size: clamp(26px, 4.4vw, 38px); }
  .lead { margin: 10px 0 0; color: var(--color-muted); max-width: 62ch; font-size: 16px; }
  .prose { max-width: 74ch; padding-top: 30px; }
  .prose h2 { font-size: 19px; margin: 28px 0 8px; }
  .prose p { margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: 15px; color: var(--color-muted); line-height: 1.7; }
  .prose a { color: var(--color-green-dark); text-decoration: underline; }
  .fineprint { font-size: 13px !important; }
</style>
